From 062cb3811edce89ac3e08eedfc521822831b1153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:38:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] efi/libstub: ignore an initrd named by the devicetree

On arm64 the kernel takes the initrd from the devicetree's /chosen node
(linux,initrd-start/end) when it is there, and only falls back to the
initrd the EFI stub loaded (LINUX_EFI_INITRD_MEDIA_GUID) while
phys_initrd_size is still 0.

The stub measures its initrd into PCR 9, but the devicetree that the
boot loader installs is not measured. On a machine whose TPM releases a
disk key only for the measured boot path (kernel, command line and initrd
in PCR 4 and 9), a changed devicetree file could name an initrd of its
own, staged somewhere in memory, and run it with all PCRs unchanged.

Delete these two properties from the devicetree the stub passes on, so
the only initrd that can run is the measured one.

Signed-off-by: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/fdt.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/fdt.c b/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/fdt.c
index 23b3543d3..a729d90ba 100644
--- a/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/fdt.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/efi/libstub/fdt.c
@@ -92,6 +92,23 @@ static efi_status_t update_fdt(void *orig_fdt, unsigned long orig_fdt_size,
 			goto fdt_set_fail;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The stub hands the kernel its initrd itself (LINUX_EFI_INITRD_MEDIA_GUID)
+	 * and measures it into PCR 9 together with the command line. An initrd
+	 * named by the devicetree takes precedence over that one, because
+	 * efi_config_parse_tables() only uses the stub's initrd while
+	 * phys_initrd_size is still 0. The devicetree itself is not measured, so
+	 * on a machine whose TPM releases a disk key for the measured boot path a
+	 * changed devicetree could run an initrd of its own choosing with the PCRs
+	 * unchanged. Drop such an initrd.
+	 */
+	if (fdt_getprop(fdt, node, "linux,initrd-start", NULL) ||
+	    fdt_getprop(fdt, node, "linux,initrd-end", NULL)) {
+		efi_warn("Ignoring the initrd named by the devicetree\n");
+		fdt_delprop(fdt, node, "linux,initrd-start");
+		fdt_delprop(fdt, node, "linux,initrd-end");
+	}
+
 	/* Add FDT entries for EFI runtime services in chosen node. */
 	node = fdt_subnode_offset(fdt, 0, "chosen");
 	fdt_val64 = cpu_to_fdt64((u64)(unsigned long)efi_system_table);
